{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/20014-steam-sale-help-me","id":20014,"title":"Steam Sale, Help. Me.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-28T19:07:02-08:00","id":20014,"title":"Steam Sale, Help. Me.","content":"I have narrowed it down to three choices, and am paralyzed with indecision.<br /> <br /> 1. The Witcher 2.<br /> 2. Dead Space 2.<br /> 3. Outlast (indie horror) and Left for Dead 2.<br /> <br /> I can only afford one of these bundles atm. Help meeeeee.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Soooo. I put this in off topic. But...its not. Help?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":863,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/863-doctor-lazarus","user":"Doctor Lazarus","date":". 11-28-2013, 10:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/863-doctor-lazarus","name":"Doctor Lazarus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-28T19:18:31-08:00","id":20020,"title":"","content":"I played Dead Space 2 all the way through and found it pretty lackluster.<br /> I only played a little of the Witcher 2, and it did seem good but it wasn't very much. The game seems to have a lot more in the way of options and choice than any of the others would.<br /> I got Outlast on the sale too, but haven't played it yet.<br /> <br /> I think Left 4 Dead would be really worth it if you had some good friends to play it with. Otherwise hedge your bets with the Witcher and wait for Outlast to go on sale again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-28T19:30:28-08:00","id":20026,"title":"","content":"Witcher, definitely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-28T19:34:46-08:00","id":20028,"title":"","content":"Gah. too many options. I got a bunch of people saying Witcher, a bunch saying Dead Space, and one that is really, really, pulling for Outlast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/863-doctor-lazarus","name":"Doctor Lazarus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-28T21:55:48-08:00","id":20093,"title":"","content":"Here's my input:<br /> <br /> First off, do not buy either the Witcher or Dead Space until they're given a special sale, or until the final day of the sale. This is a good rule to follow regardless of the game. L4D2 and Outlast complicate matters a bit, because they're specifically on sale right now, and will be for only another twelve hours. So priority one is to either settle on L4D2/Outlast, or rule them out.<br /> <br /> I would say that <b>if</b> you have a group of people who regularly play, and <b>if </b>you are interested in joining them for multiplayer, then L4D2 is a no-brainer. If multiplayer is your thing, it will give you more entertainment for your buck than any of the other games. In that case, go for it immediately. If that's<b> not</b> the case, I'd honestly recommend you pass on L4D2. Playing single-player or with randoms doesn't carry the same level of fun.<br /> <br /> As for Outlast...have you played either of the Amnesia games (Dark Descent or Machine for Pigs)? <b>If you have played them and enjoyed them</b>, then I'd say yes, get Outlast. <b>If you haven't</b>, then I'd say no, don't get Outlast. As I understand it, that's the sort of game you're dealing with here - the sort of horror game where you can't really fight the monsters, you just have to flee and hide until they stop hunting you. It's a pretty small niche within gaming - some people love it, some people find the lack of action dull, some people just find the whole thing too damn scary to be fun.<br /> <br /> So hopefully that helped to make up your mind about the above two games. Provided you didn't decide that you wanted both, I'd say that the decision between The Witcher 2 and Dead Space 2 comes down to a matter of genre preference: do you spend more of your time on single-player RPGs, or more on FPS's and horror games? Even if you like both, in practice you probably lean one way or the other, and either is a fine choice. If that doesn't help, I will say that I <i>still </i>hear good things about The Witcher 2 with some frequency, and I haven't heard similarly persistent praise for Dead Space 2.<br /> <br /> I hope this helps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":16,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","user":"Cielle","date":". 11-29-2013, 01:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"